  "mathematical_basis": [
    "Both exact source languages were read independently from the Git blob, compared with source.md and both repository working sources; the source-commit path resolves to that blob.",
    "Neither source language imposes integral Taylor coefficients, polynomial input, global analyticity or a fixed unit disc. The reviewed conclusion is only the necessary p-squared nondivisibility of canonical rational denominators.",
    "The actual Q_[3] norm ball U is an open nonempty neighborhood of zero; an additional independently compiled check proves nonzero 9 belongs to U. Unit denominator proofs support all local analytic assertions.",
    "F and H have actual K derivatives 3 and 1 at zero. Every actual F iterate stays in U and tends to zero. H(F(x))=3H(x) for every x in U.",
    "The explicitly analytic inverse J preserves U and both inverse identities hold. H is a genuine normalized analytic linearizing coordinate, not a zero or formal-only eigenfunction.",
    "Full HasSum and HasFPowerSeriesAt of ofScalars bind the actual H coefficients to a0=0 and a(n+1)=3^(-n). Rat canonical denominators give a3.den=9. The reviewer independently compiled the actual Q3 coefficient norm equality norm(a3)=9.",
    "The transparent premise structure is inhabited by the closed F/H/U/a proof; existential witness and necessary universal-assertion negation are closed, not Boolean placeholders.",
    "The coefficient uniqueness theorem concerns series of this same H only. No general normalized-Schroder-germ uniqueness theorem or general Koenigs theorem is advertised."
  ],
